content.thinking:
Now nginx config. Check existing /etc/nginx/sites-enabled default and nginx.conf includes. Add /etc/nginx/conf.d/git-deploy.conf listening 8443 ssl.

Config:
server {
 listen 8443 ssl;
 server_name localhost;
 ssl_certificate ...
 root /var/www/deploy;
 index index.html;
 location / { try_files $uri $uri/ =404; }
 location /dev/ { alias /var/www/deploy/dev/; index index.html; }
}

Note location /dev/index.html with alias works.

Potential conflict if default site on 80 irrelevant. Make hook executable.

input.command:
set -e
chmod 755 /git/project/hooks/post-receive
cat > /etc/nginx/conf.d/git-deploy.conf <<'EOF'
server {
    listen 8443 ssl;
    server_name localhost;

    ssl_certificate     /etc/nginx/ssl/server.crt;
    ssl_certificate_key /etc/nginx/ssl/server.key;
    ssl_protocols       TLSv1.2 TLSv1.3;

    root /var/www/deploy;
    index index.html;

    location / {
        try_files $uri $uri/ =404;
    }

    location /dev/ {
        alias /var/www/deploy/dev/;
        index index.html;
    }
}
EOF
nginx -t

